{"ref": "Zohar, Mishpatim 3:233", "heRef": "ספר הזהר, משפטים ג׳:רל״ג", "sectionRef": "Zohar, Mishpatim 3", "indexTitle": "Zohar", "heIndexTitle": "ספר הזהר", "categories": ["Kabbalah", "Zohar"], "next": "Zohar, Mishpatim 4", "sectionNames": ["Chapter", "Paragraph"], "versions": [{"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Vocalized Zohar, Israel 2013", "license": "unknown", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990035741170205171/NLI", "hasText": true}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "The Zohar; London, Soncino Press, 1933", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH997012945475805171/NLI", "text": "Now this verse will repay a little closer consideration. The question is, does it refer to the living or to the dead? For the beginning and the end seem to conflict with one another, the first part referring to the living and the second to the dead. We may, however, interpret thus. As long as a man is alive and walks “frowardly in the way of his heart” because the evil inclination is strong in him, making it hard for him to repent and start a new life"}], "available_versions": [{"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "The Zohar; London, Soncino Press, 1933", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH997012945475805171/NLI"}, {"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Vocalized Zohar, Israel 2013", "license": "unknown", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990035741170205171/NLI"}, {"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Sulam Edition, Jerusalem 1945", "license": "unknown", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001329911/NLI"}, {"language": "he", "languageFamilyNa